<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_scope={@current_scope}>
  <div id="terms-of-service">
    <.legal_document
      draft={false}
      eyebrow={dgettext("legal", "Using Gesttalt")}
      title={dgettext("legal", "Terms of service")}
      description={
        dgettext(
          "legal",
          "These terms describe the publishing service, early access, customer responsibilities, moderation, termination, and liability."
        )
      }
    >
      <section data-part="section">
        <h2 data-part="title">{dgettext("legal", "Contracting party and scope")}</h2>
        <p>
          Gesttalt is operated by Pedro Piñera Buendía, trading as Gesttalt, as a sole proprietor.
          The contracting party's serviceable address is Jessnerstrasse 27a, 10247 Berlin, Germany.
          These terms apply when you create an account or use the hosted publishing service. Last
          updated: 23 July 2026.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-part="section">
        <h2 data-part="title">{dgettext("legal", "Accounts")}</h2>
        <p>
          You must be at least 18 years old and able to enter a binding contract. You must provide
          accurate account information, keep credentials and connected-application secrets secure,
          and promptly report suspected misuse. You are responsible for activity performed through
          your account unless it resulted from a security failure attributable to Gesttalt.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-part="section">
        <h2 data-part="title">{dgettext("legal", "Publishing service and early access")}</h2>
        <p>
          Gesttalt provides tools to create and publish posts and pages, store images, use custom
          domains, edit themes, and publish through supported programmatic interfaces. The service
          is free during early access and does not require payment details. Gesttalt may introduce
          paid plans later, but no charge or paid renewal will begin without clear terms and your
          express order.
        </p>
        <p>
          Early access is under active development. Features may change, be unavailable, or contain
          errors. There is no guaranteed service level or continuous availability during early
          access. Gesttalt will use reasonable care in operating the service and maintaining
          backups, but you should keep an independent copy of important content.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-part="section">
        <h2 data-part="title">{dgettext("legal", "Your content and permissions")}</h2>
        <p>
          You retain ownership of content and themes you submit. You grant Gesttalt a worldwide,
          non-exclusive, royalty-free permission to host, reproduce, adapt technically, back up,
          and publicly deliver that material only as needed to operate the service at your
          direction. The permission ends when the material is deleted, subject to backup expiry and
          legal preservation duties.
        </p>
        <p>
          You must have the rights and permissions needed to submit and publish all text, images,
          code, personal information, and other material. You are responsible for connected domain
          names and for the legal notices, privacy information, and disclosures required for your
          own publication.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-part="section">
        <h2 data-part="title">{dgettext("legal", "Acceptable use")}</h2>
        <p>
          Do not use Gesttalt to publish illegal material; infringe intellectual-property, privacy,
          or personality rights; impersonate others; distribute malicious software; evade security
          controls; facilitate fraud; send unsolicited bulk messages; or threaten, exploit, or
          endanger people. Do not overload the service or interfere with another person's use.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-part="section">
        <h2 data-part="title">{dgettext("legal", "Reports and moderation")}</h2>
        <p>
          Anyone may use the <a href={~p"/report-illegal-content"}>illegal-content reporting form</a>. Gesttalt assesses
          reports diligently, objectively, and without arbitrary treatment. Moderation and
          decisions are performed by a person. Gesttalt does not use automated moderation or
          automated decision-making.
        </p>
        <p>
          Gesttalt may preserve evidence, restrict access to content, disconnect a domain, or
          suspend an account where required by law or reasonably necessary to address a material
          breach of these terms. Affected users receive a reason where the law permits it and may
          request another human review by writing to <a href="mailto:gesttalt@pepicrft.me">gesttalt@pepicrft.me</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-part="section">
        <h2 data-part="title">{dgettext("legal", "Ending the service and exporting content")}</h2>
        <p>
          You may stop using Gesttalt at any time. The permanent deletion control in
          <a href={~p"/users/settings"}>account settings</a>
          removes your account, publication, connected applications, and uploaded media. Deletion
          cannot be undone; encrypted backups expire within 30 days.
        </p>
        <p>
          If Gesttalt ordinarily terminates your account or closes the service, it will give at
          least 30 days' notice and keep access available during that period so you can copy your
          content. Immediate restriction or termination may be necessary for an urgent legal or
          security reason, a serious or repeated breach, or conduct that materially endangers
          another person or the service. Where possible, Gesttalt will still provide a reasonable
          way to retrieve lawful content.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-part="section">
        <h2 data-part="title">{dgettext("legal", "Liability")}</h2>
        <p>
          Gesttalt has unlimited liability for intent and gross negligence; injury to life, body,
          or health; guarantees expressly given; liability under the German Product Liability Act;
          and any other liability that cannot legally be limited.
        </p>
        <p>
          For ordinary negligence, Gesttalt is liable only for breach of a duty whose performance
          is essential to the contract and on whose performance you may normally rely. In that
          case, liability is limited to loss that was typical and reasonably foreseeable when the
          contract was made. This limitation does not reduce mandatory consumer rights or
          statutory rights concerning defective digital products.
        </p>
        <p>
          Gesttalt is not responsible for content you publish, external services you connect,
          internet or domain-provider failures outside Gesttalt's control, or loss caused by your
          failure to secure credentials or keep a reasonable independent copy, except to the extent
          the loss was also caused by a breach for which Gesttalt is liable under the preceding
          paragraphs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-part="section">
        <h2 data-part="title">{dgettext("legal", "Changes")}</h2>
        <p>
          Gesttalt may change these terms when reasonably necessary for legal or security
          requirements, to reflect a changed service, or to preserve a balanced contractual
          relationship. Material changes will be explained by email at least 30 days before they
          take effect. Urgent legal or security changes may take effect sooner, with notice as soon
          as reasonably possible. If you do not accept a material change, you may end the service
          and copy your content before it takes effect.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-part="section">
        <h2 data-part="title">{dgettext("legal", "Governing law and contact")}</h2>
        <p>
          German law applies, excluding its conflict-of-law rules and the United Nations Convention
          on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods. A consumer keeps any mandatory
          protection provided by the law of the country where they habitually live. Mandatory
          rules on court jurisdiction remain unaffected.
        </p>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms may be sent to <a href="mailto:gesttalt@pepicrft.me">gesttalt@pepicrft.me</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </.legal_document>
  </div>
</Layouts.app>
